/F2 20 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 768 Tm (The Industrial Revolution) Tj
/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 725 Tm (Origins) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 702 Tm (The Industrial Revolution began in Britain in the late 18th century. Britain had large) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 686.5 Tm (reserves of coal and iron ore, which fuelled early industry. The enclosure movement pushed) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 671.0 Tm (many rural workers into cities, creating a large labour force.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 650.5 Tm (Britain also had a stable government, a growing empire that supplied raw materials, and) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 635.0 Tm (banks willing to lend money to new businesses.) Tj
/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 606.5 Tm (Key Inventions) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 583.5 Tm (In 1764, James Hargreaves invented the spinning jenny, which allowed one worker to spin) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 568.0 Tm (several threads at once. James Watt improved the steam engine in 1769 by adding a separate) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 552.5 Tm (condenser.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 532.0 Tm (The power loom, patented by Edmund Cartwright in 1785, mechanised weaving. George Stephenson) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 516.5 Tm (built the Rocket, an early steam locomotive, in 1829.) Tj
