/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 760 Tm (The Factory System) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 737 Tm (The factory system brought workers and machines together under one roof. Child labour was) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 721.5 Tm (common in early textile mills, where children as young as six worked long shifts.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 701.0 Tm (The Factory Act of 1833 limited the working hours of children in textile factories and) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 685.5 Tm (introduced factory inspectors.) Tj
/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 657.0 Tm (Urbanisation) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 634.0 Tm (Urbanisation is the growth of towns and cities as people move from rural areas. Manchester) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 618.5 Tm (grew from a market town into the centre of the cotton industry. Poor sanitation in crowded) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 603.0 Tm (cities led to outbreaks of cholera.) Tj
/F2 13.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 574.5 Tm (Social Change) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 551.5 Tm (The working class emerged as a new social group of wage labourers. Luddites were textile) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 536.0 Tm (workers who destroyed machinery in protest between 1811 and 1816.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 515.5 Tm (Trade unions are organisations of workers that bargain collectively for better wages and) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 500.0 Tm (conditions. The Combination Acts of 1799 and 1800 made trade unions illegal in Britain; they) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56 484.5 Tm (were repealed in 1824.) Tj
